{"id":"translator-and-historical-edition-notes-part-7","label":"Translator and historical edition notes (part 7)","headingNoteRefs":"","context":"","kind":"commentary","blocks":[{"text":"[^n2591]: John xi. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2591"},{"text":"[^n2592]: John xi. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2592"},{"text":"[^n2593]: John xi. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2593"},{"text":"[^n2594]: John xi. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2594"},{"text":"[^n2595]: The Syriac word for Twin.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2595"},{"text":"[^n2596]: John xi. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2596"},{"text":"[^n2597]: John xi. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2597"},{"text":"[^n2598]: Arabic mil, a somewhat indefinite distance.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2598"},{"text":"[^n2599]: John xi. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2599"},{"text":"[^n2600]: John xi. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2600"},{"text":"[^n2601]: John xi. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2601"},{"text":"[^n2602]: John xi. 22.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2602"},{"text":"[^n2603]: John xi. 23.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2603"},{"text":"[^n2604]: John xi. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2604"},{"text":"[^n2605]: John xi. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2605"},{"text":"[^n2606]: John xi. 26.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2606"},{"text":"[^n2607]: John xi. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2607"},{"text":"[^n2608]: John xi. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2608"},{"text":"[^n2609]: John xi. 29.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2609"},{"text":"[^n2610]: John xi. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2610"},{"text":"[^n2611]: John xi. 31.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2611"},{"text":"[^n2612]: John xi. 32.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2612"},{"text":"[^n2613]: John xi. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2613"},{"text":"[^n2614]: This is the Syriac word (cf. the versions, and below, § 44, 44; see also Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary, ad loc).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2614"},{"text":"[^n2615]: John xi. 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2615"},{"text":"[^n2616]: John xi. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2616"},{"text":"[^n2617]: So in Syriac versions.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2617"},{"text":"[^n2618]: John xi. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2618"},{"text":"[^n2619]: John xi. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2619"},{"text":"[^n2620]: John xi. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2620"},{"text":"[^n2621]: John xi. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2621"},{"text":"[^n2622]: Borg. ms. omits some time: he hath been.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2622"},{"text":"[^n2623]: John xi. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2623"},{"text":"[^n2624]: John xi. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2624"},{"text":"[^n2625]: John xi. 42.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2625"},{"text":"[^n2626]: John xi. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2626"},{"text":"[^n2627]: John xi. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2627"},{"text":"[^n2628]: John xi. 45.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2628"},{"text":"[^n2629]: John xi. 46.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2629"},{"text":"[^n2630]: John xi. 47.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2630"},{"text":"[^n2631]: John xi. 48.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2631"},{"text":"[^n2632]: John xi. 49.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2632"},{"text":"[^n2633]: John xi. 50.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2633"},{"text":"[^n2634]: John xi. 51.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2634"},{"text":"[^n2635]: So both mss.; but the Vat. ms. had originally a reading equivalent to the text above with of omitted.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2635"},{"text":"[^n2636]: John xi. 52.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2636"},{"text":"[^n2637]: John xi. 53.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2637"},{"text":"[^n2638]: John xi. 54.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2638"},{"text":"[^n2639]: The Arabic word as printed (following Vat. ms.) means a place for monks to live in, but we should certainly restore a diacritical point over the last letter, and thus obtain another Syriac loan-word (that used here in the Peshitta), meaning town. See also Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary, ad loc.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2639"},{"text":"[^n2640]: John xi. 55.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2640"},{"text":"[^n2641]: John xi. 56.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2641"},{"text":"[^n2642]: John xi. 57.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2642"},{"text":"[^n2643]: Luke ix. 51.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2643"},{"text":"[^n2644]: The present Arabic reading in going could pretty easily arise from that assumed in the translation above.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2644"},{"text":"[^n2645]: Luke ix. 52.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2645"},{"text":"[^n2646]: This and the following verb are singular in the printed Arabic (against the versions), although Ciasca renders them plural. A copyist using a carelessly written Arabic exemplar might conceivably overlook the plural terminations. Besides, they are often omitted in Syriac mss.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2646"},{"text":"[^n2647]: cf. note, § 1, 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2647"},{"text":"[^n2648]: Luke ix. 53.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2648"},{"text":"[^n2649]: Lit. his body.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2649"},{"text":"[^n2650]: Luke ix. 54.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2650"},{"text":"[^n2651]: Luke ix. 55.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2651"},{"text":"[^n2652]: Luke ix. 56.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2652"},{"text":"[^n2653]: John xii. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2653"},{"text":"[^n2654]: cf. the Greek phrase.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2654"},{"text":"[^n2655]: John xii. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2655"},{"text":"[^n2656]: Lit. he made (cf. first note to § 38, 43, last sentence).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2656"},{"text":"[^n2657]: Mark xiv. 3a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2657"},{"text":"[^n2658]: John xii. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2658"},{"text":"[^n2659]: John xii. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2659"},{"text":"[^n2660]: John xii. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2660"},{"text":"[^n2661]: John xii. 3a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2661"},{"text":"[^n2662]: Mark xiv. 3b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2662"},{"text":"[^n2663]: John xii. 3b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2663"},{"text":"[^n2664]: John xii. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2664"},{"text":"[^n2665]: John xii. 5.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2665"},{"text":"[^n2666]: John xii. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2666"},{"text":"[^n2667]: Lit. fell (cf. § 25, 18).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2667"},{"text":"[^n2668]: Mark xiv. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2668"},{"text":"[^n2669]: Matt. xxvi. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2669"},{"text":"[^n2670]: Mark xiv. 5b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2670"},{"text":"[^n2671]: Or, spake angrily to.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2671"},{"text":"[^n2672]: Matt. xxvi. 10a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2672"},{"text":"[^n2673]: Mark xiv. 6b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2673"},{"text":"[^n2674]: John xii. 7b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2674"},{"text":"[^n2675]: John xii. 8a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2675"},{"text":"[^n2676]: Mark xiv. 7b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2676"},{"text":"[^n2677]: Matt. xxvi. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2677"},{"text":"[^n2678]: Lit. cast, as in Greek.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2678"},{"text":"[^n2679]: Mark xiv. 8b; Mark xiv. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2679"},{"text":"[^n2680]: Luke xix. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2680"},{"text":"[^n2681]: Luke xix. 29a; Matt. xxi. 1b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2681"},{"text":"[^n2682]: Matt. xxi. 2a; Mark xi. 2b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2682"},{"text":"[^n2683]: Matt. xxi. 2b; Luke xix. 30b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2683"},{"text":"[^n2684]: Sic.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2684"},{"text":"[^n2685]: Dual in Arabic.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2685"},{"text":"[^n2686]: Matt. xxi. 2c; Luke xix. 31a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2686"},{"text":"[^n2687]: Matt. xxi. 3b; Matt. xxi. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2687"},{"text":"[^n2688]: Matt. xxi. 5.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2688"},{"text":"[^n2689]: John xii. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2689"},{"text":"[^n2690]: Matt. xxi. 6a; Luke xix. 32b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2690"},{"text":"[^n2691]: Matt. xxi. 6b; Luke xix. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2691"},{"text":"[^n2692]: Luke xix. 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2692"},{"text":"[^n2693]: Mark xi. 6b; Matt. xxi. 7.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2693"},{"text":"[^n2694]: Matt. xxi. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2694"},{"text":"[^n2695]: Luke xix. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2695"},{"text":"[^n2696]: The Syriac versions have the.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2696"},{"text":"[^n2697]: Matt. xxi. 9b [or better Luke xix. 38a.].","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2697"},{"text":"[^n2698]: Mark xi. 10a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2698"},{"text":"[^n2699]: Or, and, Blessed.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2699"},{"text":"[^n2700]: The Arabic has to, but it probably represents the Syriac text with the meaning given above.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2700"},{"text":"[^n2701]: Luke xix. 38c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2701"},{"text":"[^n2702]: John xii. 12b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2702"},{"text":"[^n2703]: Lit. the heart (or, pith) of the palm. The word pith, which occurs also in the Æhiopic version (Ezek. xxvii. 25; Jubilees, ch. 16) and in Ibn-at-Tayyib’s exposition, though not in the Brit. Mus. gospel text, is perhaps used here of the inner branches from its resemblance to the post-biblical Hebrew word employed in accounts of the Feast of Tabernacles.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2703"},{"text":"[^n2704]: John xii. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2704"},{"text":"[^n2705]: Luke xix. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2705"},{"text":"[^n2706]: Luke xix. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2706"},{"text":"[^n2707]: Luke xix. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2707"},{"text":"[^n2708]: Luke xix. 42.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2708"},{"text":"[^n2709]: Lit. are found, a rendering due to the Syriac.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2709"},{"text":"[^n2710]: Luke xix. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2710"},{"text":"[^n2711]: Luke xix. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2711"},{"text":"[^n2712]: So Ciasca’s text, following Vat. ms. The other ms. has drag, which by restoring a diacritical point to the third radical would give destroy, the reading of the Syriac versions. Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary has hide.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2712"},{"text":"[^n2713]: Matt. xxi. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2713"},{"text":"[^n2714]: Matt. xxi. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2714"},{"text":"[^n2715]: John xii. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2715"},{"text":"[^n2716]: John xii. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2716"},{"text":"[^n2717]: Matt. xxi. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2717"},{"text":"[^n2718]: Matt. xxi. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2718"},{"text":"[^n2719]: Matt. xxi. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2719"},{"text":"[^n2720]: John xii. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2720"},{"text":"[^n2721]: John xii. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2721"},{"text":"[^n2722]: John xii. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2722"},{"text":"[^n2723]: John xii. 22.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2723"},{"text":"[^n2724]: John xii. 23.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2724"},{"text":"[^n2725]: John xii. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2725"},{"text":"[^n2726]: John xii. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2726"},{"text":"[^n2727]: Or, soul; or, self.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2727"},{"text":"[^n2728]: Or, soul; or, self.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2728"},{"text":"[^n2729]: John xii. 26.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2729"},{"text":"[^n2730]: John xii. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2730"},{"text":"[^n2731]: John xii. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2731"},{"text":"[^n2732]: John xii. 29.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2732"},{"text":"[^n2733]: John xii. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2733"},{"text":"[^n2734]: John xii. 31.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2734"},{"text":"[^n2735]: John xii. 32.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2735"},{"text":"[^n2736]: John xii. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2736"},{"text":"[^n2737]: John xii. 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2737"},{"text":"[^n2738]: John xii. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2738"},{"text":"[^n2739]: John xii. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2739"},{"text":"[^n2740]: Luke xvii. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2740"},{"text":"[^n2741]: Luke xvii. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2741"},{"text":"[^n2742]: Luke xxi. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2742"},{"text":"[^n2743]: Luke xxi. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2743"},{"text":"[^n2744]: i.e., used to come.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2744"},{"text":"[^n2745]: Matt. xxiii. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2745"},{"text":"[^n2746]: Matt. xxiii. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2746"},{"text":"[^n2747]: Matt. xxiii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2747"},{"text":"[^n2748]: Matt. xxiii. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2748"},{"text":"[^n2749]: Or, touch.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2749"},{"text":"[^n2750]: Matt. xxiii. 5a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2750"},{"text":"[^n2751]: Mark xii. 37b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2751"},{"text":"[^n2752]: Mark xii. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2752"},{"text":"[^n2753]: Mark xii. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2753"},{"text":"[^n2754]: Matt. xxiii. 5b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2754"},{"text":"[^n2755]: Matt. xxiii. 7b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2755"},{"text":"[^n2756]: Mark xii. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2756"},{"text":"[^n2757]: The Syriac word means on the pretext of as well as because of (cf. § 50, 11, note).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2757"},{"text":"[^n2758]: Matt. xxiii. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2758"},{"text":"[^n2759]: This word is not spelled in the ordinary way. Doubtless we should supply two diacritical points and read, with the Syriac versions, My master.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2759"},{"text":"[^n2760]: Matt. xxiii. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2760"},{"text":"[^n2761]: cf. Peshitta.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2761"},{"text":"[^n2762]: Matt. xxiii. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2762"},{"text":"[^n2763]: Matt. xxiii. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2763"},{"text":"[^n2764]: Matt. xxiii. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2764"},{"text":"[^n2765]: Luke xi. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2765"},{"text":"[^n2766]: Matt. xxiii. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2766"},{"text":"[^n2767]: Syriac, same as in § 40, 35; Arabic different.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2767"},{"text":"[^n2768]: Matt. xxiii. 13a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2768"},{"text":"[^n2769]: Luke xi. 52a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2769"},{"text":"[^n2770]: Matt. xxiii. 13b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2770"},{"text":"[^n2771]: Matt. xxiii. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2771"},{"text":"[^n2772]: Adopting the reading of Borg. ms. (cf. next verse).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2772"},{"text":"[^n2773]: Perhaps this reading is due to the easy confusion of d and r in Syriac; but it might also conceivably be a corruption of the Arabic word in the next clause. It occurs also in the text of Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2773"},{"text":"[^n2774]: Doubtless the Arabic word should be read as a monosyllable, as in Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2774"},{"text":"[^n2775]: Matt. xxiii. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2775"},{"text":"[^n2776]: See § 10, 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2776"},{"text":"[^n2777]: Matt. xxiii. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2777"},{"text":"[^n2778]: Matt. xxiii. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2778"},{"text":"[^n2779]: See § 10, 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2779"},{"text":"[^n2780]: Matt. xxiii. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2780"},{"text":"[^n2781]: Matt. xxiii. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2781"},{"text":"[^n2782]: Matt. xxiii. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2782"},{"text":"[^n2783]: Matt. xxiii. 22.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2783"},{"text":"[^n2784]: Matt. xxiii. 23.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2784"},{"text":"[^n2785]: Matt. xxiii. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2785"},{"text":"[^n2786]: The Arabic word as printed gives no suitable sense. Either the last radical has been omitted, or the last two radicals have exchanged places.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2786"},{"text":"[^n2787]: Matt. xxiii. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2787"},{"text":"[^n2788]: Matt. xxiii. 26.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2788"},{"text":"[^n2789]: Matt. xxiii. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2789"},{"text":"[^n2790]: Lit. are seen.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2790"},{"text":"[^n2791]: Matt. xxiii. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2791"},{"text":"[^n2792]: Luke xi. 45.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2792"},{"text":"[^n2793]: Luke xi. 46.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2793"},{"text":"[^n2794]: Or, touch.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2794"},{"text":"[^n2795]: Matt. xxiii. 29a; Luke xi. 47b; Matt. xxiii. 29b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2795"},{"text":"[^n2796]: Matt. xxiii. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2796"},{"text":"[^n2797]: Matt. xxiii. 31.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2797"},{"text":"[^n2798]: Matt. xxiii. 32.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2798"},{"text":"[^n2799]: Lit. boundary or limit.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2799"},{"text":"[^n2800]: Matt. xxiii. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2800"},{"text":"[^n2801]: Matt. xxiii. 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2801"},{"text":"[^n2802]: cf. 8, 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2802"},{"text":"[^n2803]: Matt. xxiii. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2803"},{"text":"[^n2804]: Or, earth.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2804"},{"text":"[^n2805]: Or, sanctuary.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2805"},{"text":"[^n2806]: Matt. xxiii. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2806"},{"text":"[^n2807]: See § 1, 49, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2807"},{"text":"[^n2808]: Matt. xxiii. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2808"},{"text":"[^n2809]: Matt. xxiii. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2809"},{"text":"[^n2810]: Matt. xxiii. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2810"},{"text":"[^n2811]: John xii. 42.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2811"},{"text":"[^n2812]: Lit. become.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2812"},{"text":"[^n2813]: John xii. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2813"},{"text":"[^n2814]: John xii. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2814"},{"text":"[^n2815]: John xii. 45.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2815"},{"text":"[^n2816]: John xii. 46.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2816"},{"text":"[^n2817]: The text as it stands ought to mean I am a light. I am come; but it is a word-for-word reproduction of the Peshitta, and should therefore doubtless be rendered as above.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2817"},{"text":"[^n2818]: John xii. 47.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2818"},{"text":"[^n2819]: Or, to save the world (cf. § 1, 78, note).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2819"},{"text":"[^n2820]: John xii. 48.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2820"},{"text":"[^n2821]: See § 20, 28, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2821"},{"text":"[^n2822]: John xii. 49.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2822"},{"text":"[^n2823]: Not the same word.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2823"},{"text":"[^n2824]: Not the same word.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2824"},{"text":"[^n2825]: John xii. 50.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2825"},{"text":"[^n2826]: Luke xi. 53.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2826"},{"text":"[^n2827]: So Ciasca, following Vat. ms. The true reading, however, is probably that underlying the Borg. ms. If we restore diacritical points to the radical letters we get deceiving (cf. § 41, 31), an alternative meaning (or the word laying wait for, used in the Peshitta. The Arabic follows the Peshitta very closely in this and the following verse.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2827"},{"text":"[^n2828]: Luke xi. 54.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2828"},{"text":"[^n2829]: Luke xii. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2829"},{"text":"[^n2830]: Luke xii. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2830"},{"text":"[^n2831]: Luke xii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2831"},{"text":"[^n2832]: John xii. 36b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2832"},{"text":"[^n2833]: John xii. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2833"},{"text":"[^n2834]: John xii. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2834"},{"text":"[^n2835]: John xii. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2835"},{"text":"[^n2836]: John xii. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2836"},{"text":"[^n2837]: John xii. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2837"},{"text":"[^n2838]: Matt. xxiv. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2838"},{"text":"[^n2839]: Or, and shewed.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2839"},{"text":"[^n2840]: Mark xiii. 1b; Luke xxi. 5b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2840"},{"text":"[^n2841]: Matt. xxiv. 2a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2841"},{"text":"[^n2842]: Luke xix. 43a; Luke xix. 44b [or rather Matt. xxiv. 2b, or Mark xiii. 2b].","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2842"},{"text":"[^n2843]: Mark xiv. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2843"},{"text":"[^n2844]: Lit. before two days would be (cf. Sin. and above, § 39, 1, note).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2844"},{"text":"[^n2845]: cf. § 41, 16, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2845"},{"text":"[^n2846]: Mark xiv. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2846"},{"text":"[^n2847]: Mark xiii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2847"},{"text":"[^n2848]: Luke xxi. 7b; Matt. xxiv. 3b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2848"},{"text":"[^n2849]: Matt. xxiv. 4a; Luke xvii. 22b; Matt. xxiv. 4b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2849"},{"text":"[^n2850]: Matt. xxiv. 5a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2850"},{"text":"[^n2851]: Luke xxi. 8b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2851"},{"text":"[^n2852]: Mark xiii. 6b; Luke xxi. 8c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2852"},{"text":"[^n2853]: Mark xiii. 7a; Matt. xxiv. 7b; Luke xxi. 9b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2853"},{"text":"[^n2854]: Or, that ye be, if we suppose the present text to have resulted from the loss of the second of two alifs.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2854"},{"text":"[^n2855]: Matt. xxiv. 7a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2855"},{"text":"[^n2856]: Luke xxi. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2856"},{"text":"[^n2857]: Or, omit that.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2857"},{"text":"[^n2858]: Matt. xxiv. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2858"},{"text":"[^n2859]: Luke xxi. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2859"},{"text":"[^n2860]: Luke xxi. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2860"},{"text":"[^n2861]: Mark xiii. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2861"},{"text":"[^n2862]: Luke xii. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2862"},{"text":"[^n2863]: Mark xiii. 11b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2863"},{"text":"[^n2864]: Luke xxi. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2864"},{"text":"[^n2865]: Luke xxi. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2865"},{"text":"[^n2866]: The Arabic text lacks a letter.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2866"},{"text":"[^n2867]: Borg. ms. reads you the fruits of wisdom.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2867"},{"text":"[^n2868]: Matt. xxiv. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2868"},{"text":"[^n2869]: Matt. xxiv. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2869"},{"text":"[^n2870]: See § 25, 17, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2870"},{"text":"[^n2871]: Luke xxi. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2871"},{"text":"[^n2872]: Luke xxi. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2872"},{"text":"[^n2873]: Luke xxi. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2873"},{"text":"[^n2874]: Or, possess.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2874"},{"text":"[^n2875]: Matt. xxiv. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2875"},{"text":"[^n2876]: So the Arabic text; but it doubtless simply represents the Syriac, which here agrees with the Greek.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2876"},{"text":"[^n2877]: Matt. xxiv. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2877"},{"text":"[^n2878]: Matt. xxiv. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2878"},{"text":"[^n2879]: Matt. xxiv. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2879"},{"text":"[^n2880]: So the Arabic text; but it doubtless simply represents the Syriac, which here agrees with the Greek.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2880"},{"text":"[^n2881]: Luke xxi. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2881"},{"text":"[^n2882]: Luke xxi. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2882"},{"text":"[^n2883]: Luke xxi. 22.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2883"},{"text":"[^n2884]: Matt. xxiv. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2884"},{"text":"[^n2885]: So Vat. ms., following the Peshitta. Ciasca follows Borg. ms., which by a change of diacritical points has the hardly grammatical reading, see that it is the desolation, the unclean thing spoken of. Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary supports Vat. ms.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2885"},{"text":"[^n2886]: Matt. xxiv. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2886"},{"text":"[^n2887]: Mark xiii. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2887"},{"text":"[^n2888]: Mark xiii. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2888"},{"text":"[^n2889]: Luke xxi. 23.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2889"},{"text":"[^n2890]: Luke xxi. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2890"},{"text":"[^n2891]: This word has a Syriac meaning given to it. In Arabic it means war.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2891"},{"text":"[^n2892]: Mark xiii. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2892"},{"text":"[^n2893]: Matt. xxiv. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2893"},{"te